<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply cut in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply cut in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said it withdrew liquidity from the money market in the week to Jan 27 to offset a fall in notes in circulation. FX reserves rose.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   436.075 ( + 1.761)</p>
<p>Advances against pledged security  14.724 ( - 1.336)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.967 ( - 0.050)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   24.861 ( - 0.010)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	  95.968 ( - 3.742)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   445.474 ( - 7.851)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
